{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins","id":1341402,"title":"Strix origins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-14T22:33:59-07:00","id":1341402,"title":"Strix origins","content":"I was wondering if their is origins of where the strix come from? I know their is no definitive origin is chronicles of darkness but i saw in a couple forum that the Strix come from the lower depths? But could never find the source","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T22:50:39-07:00","id":1341404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightsyko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins#post1341402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if their is origins of where the strix come from? I know their is no definitive origin is chronicles of darkness but i saw in a couple forum that the Strix come from the lower depths? But could never find the source</div> </div> </div> </div>They come from a dark place that nobody ever seems to return from, steal life and corrupt other things into things that steal life, and are seemingly attracted to things going badly wrong, all of which make them fairly easily associated with other probable incursions from the Lower Depths, like the servants of the Maeljin (which 1e's book on the Inferno, the original primary Lower Depth of the setting, identifies as close enough to its sort of demons for that book's purposes) or the Cthonic Gods (&quot;the Underworld is provably the worst-damaged of the Fallen Worlds&quot; is a thing Dave Brookshaw has observed) or the Judges of Duat (which drain the manifest energy of magical relics through their proxies and were only too ready to feed a tenth of the world to an oblivion-goddess).<br /> <br /> Wherever they came from originally, modern Strix are native to the material plane and possibly have many different origins blended into their pedigree through diablerie and magical mitosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T02:01:34-07:00","id":1341414,"title":"","content":"Mage gets its a bit into the metaphysics of the Lower Depths, but it\u2019s obviously not relevant from a VTR perspective. General rule of thumb is any lower depth realm lacks some aspect of reality, and the beings from that realm hunger for it. Strix seem to hunger for life. If you\u2019re familiar with the platonic cosmology of Mage, the Lower Depths are thought of as being as far beneath the Phenomenal World as the Phenomenal World is beneath the Supernal, defined by the absences of certain world defining truths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T05:47:49-07:00","id":1341428,"title":"","content":"In VtR 2e core it's described how they can open up a portal to a realm of darkness (known as Dis in the fandom) at Shadow Potency 10. It's that realm that's described as a Lower Depth.<br /> I want to add that it may not be their place of origin; it might only be a place highly connected to the Strix. It would not be the first time a type of entity in CofD isn't native to their associated realm, like ghosts and the Underworld, or True Fae and Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T12:24:51-07:00","id":1341490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1341414#post1341414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you\u2019re familiar with the platonic cosmology of Mage, the Lower Depths are thought of as being as far beneath the Phenomenal World as the Phenomenal World is beneath the Supernal, defined by the absences of certain world defining truths.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting connection that I'd never noticed before.<br /> <br /> Plato mentions shadows and poetry as among the least real things. So we're talking about things that are not ontologically grounded -- things whose existence depends on other things (think of reflections, illusions, or other epiphenomena). The Strix are made of smoke and shadow, which is exactly the kind of transient byproduct that Plato would have identified as being &quot;least real&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: technically smoke has its own existence, but whatever, technicalities are for nerds and philosophy majors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 10-15-2019, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T15:11:36-07:00","id":1341510,"title":"","content":"Interesting a high level game in the world of Dis could be fun to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T16:16:12-07:00","id":1341516,"title":"","content":"Rose's book <i>Hijack</i> lists one possible origin that was used by the devs, but it's CofD, there's No True Canon.<br /> <br /> The Strix might always have existed, long before humanity did, but humans were the ones who first pushed the shadows back by taming fire and building houses with thresholds and running water, so they hate humanity in particular.<br /> <br /> According to Ovid (a Roman poet and dubiously-accurate mythographer), they might have once been humans, who tried to achieve immortality through magic. If that's the case, in the CofD-verse, their attempt succeeded at a horrific cost, leaving them with no trace of their former humanity except a lingering hatred for what they've lost and can never have again.<br /> <br /> They might be ephemerals from another world, who ended up non-ephemeral in our world (cf Hedge Ghosts) and found that they can use human life-force like Essence to keep themselves here.<br /> <br /> They might be exactly the same thing as the Beast is, just with nothing holding it back: the remains of draugar whose souls survived the destruction of their bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T11:44:33-07:00","id":1341669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightsyko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1341510#post1341510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting a high level game in the world of Dis could be fun to run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's an idea:<br /> <br /> The local Ordo Dracul trapped a bunch of Strix in jars, wired them up together, and connected them to a full length obsidian mirror in a specially chosen Wyrm's Nest. They perform a ritual which harness the Strix to turn the mirror into a gateway to Dis. They send ghouls, humans, neonates, animals, robots, and anyone and anything they can through to explore. The subjects are mounted with cameras and tethered with a cable that can be used to drag them back and sends telemetry. Subjects usually don't get very far before being killed or possessed by Strix, but that's fine; the experiment keeps burning through the Strix in the jars and replacements are always welcome.<br /> <br /> The Prince doesn't know what they are up to, but they dispose of problematic kindred and kine for him and in exchange he doesn't ask where they are going. However they are running out of subjects faster than he supplies them, and have started abducting subjects that are the least likely to be noticed. What happens if they accidentally take someone with powerful connections?<br /> <br /> Despite the Ordo Dracul's best efforts to shield the project, other Strix have started to sense something happening; more and more Strix are being spotted in the neighborhood where the Wyrm's Nest is located. They aren't attacking yet, just searching. What will happen if they find the gateway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-16-2019, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T17:01:50-07:00","id":1341741,"title":"","content":"As said there is no definite answer, but two things that are sometimes hinted at which I find interesting.<br /> <br /> First Strix are what came before Vampires, the origins of one or all of the clans actually lie with the Strix.<br /> <br /> Second the Strix are what remains of a lost Clan and now they seek revenge maybe with a connection to VII. This is especially implied in the Ventrue Clan Book. (At least it's how I red it)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1341516#post1341516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose's book <i>Hijack</i> lists one possible origin that was used by the devs, but it's CofD, there's No True Canon.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> What exactly is the book you revere to here if you don't mind me asking. Because I have no clue^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T22:10:45-07:00","id":1341787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1341741#post1341741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is the book you revere to here if you don't mind me asking. Because I have no clue^^</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/278072/HIJACK-The-Writers-Guide-to-the-Strix\" target=\"_blank\">This one!</a> Currently on sale for Halloween, even. It's mostly a bunch of dev notes on the Strix and how to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T15:34:47-07:00","id":1342586,"title":"","content":"I was wandering what will happen if a vampire commit amaranth on a vampire that possesed by a strix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25728-marios_tzi","name":"Marios_Tzi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T20:42:03-08:00","id":1348140,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, as I've stated before, introducing The Strix was a huge mistake. Spirits who crave life (blood,) who look for dead bodies to possess. And....<br /> <br /> As is obvious to original VtM players, Requiem was an attempt to fix the mistakes of the original game. Namely, to leave the origins of vampirism and The Clans ambiguous, so Story Tellers could create their own mythologies.<br /> <br /> But, apparently, there was a legion of fans who read the old meta-plot as if it was a novel, and read the awful franchise &quot;novels,&quot; who hated Requiem.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;Onyx,&quot; or whatever WW is called now mashed VtM and VtR together, to rry to make to old Alpha Nerds and new nerds happy. It's a thankless task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","user":"Illuminostro","date":". 11-12-2019, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T03:38:31-08:00","id":1348205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1348140#post1348140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, as I've stated before, introducing The Strix was a huge mistake. Spirits who crave life (blood,) who look for dead bodies to possess. And....<br /> <br /> As is obvious to original VtM players, Requiem was an attempt to fix the mistakes of the original game. Namely, to leave the origins of vampirism and The Clans ambiguous, so Story Tellers could create their own mythologies.<br /> <br /> But, apparently, there was a legion of fans who read the old meta-plot as if it was a novel, and read the awful franchise &quot;novels,&quot; who hated Requiem.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;Onyx,&quot; or whatever WW is called now mashed VtM and VtR together, to rry to make to old Alpha Nerds and new nerds happy. It's a thankless task.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Requiem did was presenting multiple optional origins for both vampires on a whole as well as the individual Clans. Neither of them might be true. Strix are similarly hinted as the origin of fleshy Kindred, but that's also optional. That <i>you</i> assume that it's the canon origin for vampires is not indicative of any VtR/VtM mash up.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, if they did want to bring in the VtM crowd, wouldn't they try for an origin story that is even remotely close to how it was in Masquerade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T05:38:32-08:00","id":1348238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1348140#post1348140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, as I've stated before, introducing The Strix was a huge mistake. Spirits who crave life (blood,) who look for dead bodies to possess. And....<br /> <br /> As is obvious to original VtM players, Requiem was an attempt to fix the mistakes of the original game. Namely, to leave the origins of vampirism and The Clans ambiguous, so Story Tellers could create their own mythologies.<br /> <br /> But, apparently, there was a legion of fans who read the old meta-plot as if it was a novel, and read the awful franchise &quot;novels,&quot; who hated Requiem.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;Onyx,&quot; or whatever WW is called now mashed VtM and VtR together, to rry to make to old Alpha Nerds and new nerds happy. It's a thankless task.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't mistake new antagonists or story hooks for metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T16:33:21-08:00","id":1348746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1348140#post1348140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, as I've stated before,</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. You have stated it before. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As is obvious to original VtM players, </div> </div> </div>I think the guide to the Strix says that they chose to go further with the Strix in part because they are the least VtM aspect of VtR. <br /> <br /> I will say, I do agree that not many other possible sources of vampirism have been explored, and that could be really fun. Maybe they could be expansions of the current setting, but they could also be shards.<br /> <br /> I'd be into some exploration of The Deep Ones, or the Mirror from that one short story that gets mentioned in CB Nosferatu, that I'm pretty sure is implied to be the Mekhet origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T21:16:27-08:00","id":1348786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1348746#post1348746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say, I do agree that not many other possible sources of vampirism have been explored, and that could be really fun. Maybe they could be expansions of the current setting, but they could also be shards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely agreed! I've been playing around with some alternate origins along these lines, inspired by <i>Requiem for Rome</i>'s origin mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T22:32:17-08:00","id":1348792,"title":"","content":"Are you talking about the Brohers Worm? Or were there other origin stories in RfR?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T09:15:56-08:00","id":1348873,"title":"","content":"The Brothers Worm, Romulus and Remus, Ishtar and Lilith, etc. (None of which are presented as true in the modern-historian sense, but rather as true in the Roman-historian sense, conveying general moral truths through mythology rather than the specific details of what happened on specific dates.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T14:54:56-08:00","id":1348935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1341428#post1341428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or True Fae and Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can I read more about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T15:00:59-08:00","id":1348937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"http