st\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I read more about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Am on mobile and site:-type Google searches were failing me, but: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1328698-i-wish-ctl-allowed-you-to-confront-your-keeper?p=1329981#post1329981\">here it is.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T15:41:25-08:00","id":1348952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1348140#post1348140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, as I've stated before, introducing The Strix was a huge mistake. Spirits who crave life (blood,) who look for dead bodies to possess. And....<br /> <br /> As is obvious to original VtM players, Requiem was an attempt to fix the mistakes of the original game. Namely, to leave the origins of vampirism and The Clans ambiguous, so Story Tellers could create their own mythologies.<br /> <br /> But, apparently, there was a legion of fans who read the old meta-plot as if it was a novel, and read the awful franchise &quot;novels,&quot; who hated Requiem.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;Onyx,&quot; or whatever WW is called now mashed VtM and VtR together, to rry to make to old Alpha Nerds and new nerds happy. It's a thankless task.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are somewhat correct in that this would have been a terrible thing if it had happened. We can count ourselves fortunate it didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T00:25:13-08:00","id":1349015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1348949#post1348949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am on mobile and site:-type Google searches were failing me, but: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1328698-i-wish-ctl-allowed-you-to-confront-your-keeper?p=1329981#post1329981\">here it is.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I don't want to derail a Vampire thread much, so I just want to ask if there's anything more about this is Changeling 2e (which I don't have)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T05:31:54-08:00","id":1349052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349015#post1349015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! I don't want to derail a Vampire thread much, so I just want to ask if there's anything more about this is Changeling 2e (which I don't have)?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far the gist of it is in the parts of the antagonists chapter describing the True Fae and the Huntsmen:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the True Fae retreat from the corners of Arcadia to hold court and play their games, the land returns to what it once was. Sometimes escaping changelings stumble across these empty realms before they cross into the Hedge, these undeveloped lands devoid of living civilization, a theatre stage with scattered props and sets but no lights or actors. Most often, changelings view them as cold woods, chilled enough to see their breath illumined in moon- and starlight, a midnight land rife with barrow mounds and watchful eyes. These eyes are both hunter and hunted, air and darkness assuming thought and form by will or whim. They are the Huntsmen: They were in Arcadia before the Gentry, and they will be there after the Gentry leave.<br /> <br /> But in this time and place, the Gentry rule the lands beyond the Hedge, and even those verderers of the woods must acknowledge their authority. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deep in the mists of forgotten time, the Fae bargained with Arcadia itself, declaring that they would exist \u2014 that they would own the land entire and claim it as a vessel for their Wyrd, dreams, and facets, in exchange for a web of arcane rules so complex no one of them could ever know them all. At their core, the Fae are ravenous beings that must <u>possess.</u> They want, and in their all-consuming wanting they strike bargains to sate their desires, whether for slaves, kingdoms, secrets, or spoils. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T06:10:36-08:00","id":1349060,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> wow!! So I guess that definitely means the Arcadia ruled by the Gentry and the Supernal Realm of Arcadia are NOT the same place. (I read in Imperial Mysteries that they were.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T06:57:33-08:00","id":1349064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349052#post1349052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far the gist of it is in the parts of the antagonists chapter describing the True Fae and the Huntsmen...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! It\u2019s very evocative, and goes a long way to make the Gentry feel more alien or indifferent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T21:48:40-08:00","id":1349277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349060#post1349060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> wow!! So I guess that definitely means the Arcadia ruled by the Gentry and the Supernal Realm of Arcadia are NOT the same place. (I read in Imperial Mysteries that they were.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to terribly derail the thread, but I have got to admit the way your mind seemingly plays hopscotch with information is fascinating and <i>frustrating</i>.<br /> <br /> Anyways, tying this around back on to point, the Strix nativity or non-nativity to either Dis or the living world is a weird thing-either they're the spirits of humanity, spurned by their progenitors, or they're emanations of a realm starved for Vitae. Reality lies somewhere in between, and honestly with that being the fact, the reality of their position in regards to either is minimally important. It takes something outside of context to really make the origin change the way you look at them-the Strix originating from Duat would be wild in a way Dis or Humanity doesn't deliver.<br /> <br /> Unlike the colonization of the Strangers or the cruel devouring of refugees in the way of the Underworld, the origin of the Strix primarily matters in regard to the flavor of horror you want to deliver. Their more-human origins causes self-reflection, their less-reflective origins emphasize a self vs world-and-nature argument, and part of Vampires conflict is that they lack matters that allow them to wholly pin things on an outside metaphysic and an internal emotional void that now translates over into the Vitae, and the catch to that is that it kind of depends on the arguments of the players and the Storyteller in particular.<br /> <br /> I mean, otherwise, the origin of the Strix is a non-point, since their Gordian Knot seems to just be inherent most of the time, and the narratives they present justifying it are just tales to tell the kid before putting them to sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T22:35:52-08:00","id":1349285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349060#post1349060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> wow!! So I guess that definitely means the Arcadia ruled by the Gentry and the Supernal Realm of Arcadia are NOT the same place. (I read in Imperial Mysteries that they were.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries answers &quot;Are the two Arcadias the same place?&quot; with &quot;It's complicated.&quot; The Old Gods of Thistle occupied a weird recurrent blur in the cosmology between Dhatu and Emanation Realm, which is an important difference when the Supernal will annihilate you without a filter and Faerie simply has terms of hospitality alongside a certain level of inherent environmental hostility. In both editions there was wiggle-room for the opposite answers to that question, but 1e leaned slightly toward &quot;yes&quot; and 2e leans slightly toward &quot;no,&quot; partially because the narrative angle that 1e leaned towards has fallen out of focus in favor of the more prosaic explanation for why faeries make their bargains.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back on the Strix, I feel it's worth pointing out Rose's old &quot;vampirism is a wound&quot; analogy in combination with the fact that historically the Strix have never claimed to be responsible for <i>vampirism</i>, only <i>the Beast</i>. (It's never just one thing, is it?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T06:36:39-08:00","id":1349323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349285#post1349285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on the Strix, I feel it's worth pointing out Rose's old &amp;quot;vampirism is a wound&amp;quot; analogy in combination with the fact that historically the Strix have never claimed to be responsible for <i>vampirism</i>, only <i>the Beast</i>. (It's never just one thing, is it?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind this. Vampirism itself is the injury, the Beast is a infected, festering wound, and Strix are both cause and continued agitator for that infection. Then I wonder what might vampirism be without an infected wound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T06:56:36-08:00","id":1349326,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> one of the guys I play with also runs an Exalted game, and he told me in his headcanon the True Fae are a group of Fair Folk nobles from Exalted who get lost in a Wyld storm and end up in the Chronicles of Darkness universe. I know they would never do that because they don't want to do crossovers between the universes, but I thought it sounded interesting. Also, I've never actually played Changeling: the Lost, but it sounds like a really cool contrast to Changeling: the Dreaming. Much darker in tone, more like Grimm's Fairy Tales.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I just realized this was a thread about the origins of the Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T08:26:03-08:00","id":1349343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349323#post1349323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can get behind this. Vampirism itself is the injury, the Beast is a infected, festering wound, and Strix are both cause and continued agitator for that infection. Then I wonder what might vampirism be without an infected wound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm not sure about that. I remember that Rose once mentioned that perhaps what we consider as the banes of the Beast- such as sunlight or fire- may very well be protective means, just like pain tells us that we are doing something bad for our body. A vampire without the Beast will be a vampire without those bane, and that was hinted to be a very, very bad thing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T08:59:22-08:00","id":1349348,"title":"","content":"So what, then, are those banes (and the Beast?) protecting vampires from, do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T11:21:00-08:00","id":1349383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349326#post1349326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry. I just realized this was a thread about the origins of the Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey dude, I enjoyed the tangent. I got the CtL book for my partner and haven't read it because she's planning to run a game, so I'm really starved of lore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349277#post1349277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the reality of their position in regards to either is minimally important. It takes something outside of context to really make the origin change the way you look at them... the origin of the Strix primarily matters in regard to the flavor of horror you want to deliver. Their more-human origins causes self-reflection,.. I mean, otherwise, the origin of the Strix is a non-point, since their Gordian Knot seems to just be inherent most of the time, and the narratives they present justifying it are just tales to tell the kid before putting them to sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the problem that the Strix present in-game is &quot;serial killing possession demon&quot;, and in terms of conflict, their origin doesn't change this problem. No matter what, they're serial killing possession demons. You're right that the choice of origin advances certain themes in the VtR game, but I think the choice is also important for how STs portray the Strix. Like, if I'm playing a spurned human spirit, I'll be giving a different mood than if I am playing a sentient void (kind of like the Spectres from His Dark Materials). And I'm going to make different choices as well.<br /> <br /> They're hungry hateful things, but we(I) need an origin for characterization purposes. In my game, I have a Strix targeting one of my PCs' younger siblings. But I literally could not figure out how to guide it's actions without an intelligible motivation. The story-planning problem, presented by the Strix was <i>Which particular choice does this </i><i>hateful, sadistic, jealous thing that directs cruelty towards children and their caretakers make next? </i>If your Strix doesn't have some master plan, and is only acting out of sadistic jealousy, we(I) need more information to determine the next action. This was before Rose's origin had come out, and I came up with a plague that wiped out a village's children.<br /> <br /> I love Rose's origin, but I think that any choice of origin needs to serve the role that the Strix play in your particular story. For my story, it was the emotional residue of a thousand babies dying painfully. It was the <i>right</i> answer, relative to this particular story, because it helped me to coherently guide the character's actions in a way that wasn't just meta-gaming. With a particular origin in mind, I can drop a lot of smaller facts and actions that hint at some larger picture. Even if the origin never comes out, the story ends up being much fuller.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349285#post1349285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel it's worth pointing out Rose's old &quot;vampirism is a wound&quot; analogy</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this conception. I'd been thinking of it as &quot;something that happens when something goes very wrong&quot;. But it brings in a weird, almost Aristotelian essentialism that I don't really like. I think framing it as a wound is much better than as a deviation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 11-18-2019, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T11:46:32-08:00","id":1349387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349348#post1349348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what, then, are those banes (and the Beast?) protecting vampires from, do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still working on it, but probably from becoming something in the style of Amoniel (that is, something in the style of an &quot;angel drenched in blood&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T11:47:51-08:00","id":1349388,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24634\" data-vbnamecard=\"24634\">DubiousRuffian</a> happy to help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Hope you enjoy her game.<br /> <br /> My personal theory is that the Strix are the children of an owl goddess (Lilith?) who was one of the original gods of Pangaea and who was banished to Dis after the Fall of Pangaea. Unfortunately, this is contradicted by a statement in Dark Eras that there were Strix-possessed bloodsucking corpses running around before the Fall, but I still like it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> hopscotch, girl <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:08:27-08:00","id":1349393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349388#post1349388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My personal theory is that the Strix are the children of an owl goddess (Lilith?) who was one of the original gods of Pangaea and who was banished to Dis after the Fall of Pangaea. Unfortunately, this is contradicted by a statement in Dark Eras that there were Strix-possessed bloodsucking corpses running around before the Fall, but I still like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the only thing you need to change is that Owl/Shadow/Lilith was banished to Dis <i>before</i> Pangaea fell. Wolf shattered a lot of his kin during that time, it won't be unlikely that she found escape and faked her death (or died and then escaped) while hiding in Dis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:30:26-08:00","id":1349402,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> thank you!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:40:23-08:00","id":1349409,"title":"","content":"It's also possible that Lilith/Owl simply was shattered by Wolf before his end, making the Strix a Host.<br /> Strix are thematically and mechanically similar to Hosts, with how they take over humans, and how they can eat each other to get more powerful as well as split up into multiple lesser beings. What differs mechanically is their traits, but most of them can be explained as being adjusted for VtR instead of WtF. Even their shadowy Vitae could actually be a type of Essence of vampiric resonances and made visible as a quirk of this particular Host. Thematically speaking they differ from most Hosts in that they have nothing to do with the Gauntlet, but nothing says all Hosts need to focus on that. The connection to a Lower Depths realm is also atypical of Hosts, but that's something Owl might've found before her shattering, and the resulting connection between her Shards and Dis might be the reason behind any differences between Strix and other Hosts.<br /> <br /> It's not my preferred take, but it makes a lot more sense to me than Strix being the spirits of humanity. Though I have to admit I haven't read the text and don't know if or how Rose explained Strix not being ephemeral, not being in the Shadow, not using Essence, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T13:01:29-08:00","id":1349420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349409#post1349409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I have to admit I haven't read the text and don't know if or how Rose explained Strix not being ephemeral, not being in the Shadow, not using Essence, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>No deep lore on that part (since it's written from the perspective of a vampire, not a woof or spirit expert), but my explanation would be\u2014when Humanity changed (in the Fall), we stopped creating &quot;human essence&quot;, which is why we don't make motes and human-spirits and such. And the Owls were starving. Some ate other essences and became magath, but some found a way to rip essence out of living humans themselves\u2014much later, Roman-era vampires called it &quot;essentia vitae&quot;, the stuff of life, and that got shortened to &quot;Vitae&quot;.<br /> <br /> But of course, there's no Vitae in the Hisil. In this scenario, maybe Dis is a fragment of the Border Marches split apart in the Sundering? The ones that would become the Strix stayed there, making it their home and emerging from time to time to go Fleshside and hunt for Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T13:47:46-08:00","id":1349436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341402-strix-origins?p=1349409#post1349409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strix not being ephemeral, not being in the Shadow, not using Essence, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know absolutely nothing about Werewolf or the lore surrounding spirits. So this is my take:<br /> <br /> There was an Enlightenment philosopher, Rousseau, who thought that humans literally changed their natures by entering into civilization. That the ability to change our own natures is an essential part of what it is to be human. I like to think that in the Chronicles, Rousseau was correct.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, it would make some sense that our spirits would have the ability to change their natures as well. So when we changed our natures, our spirits said &quot;What? No, fuck that. And fuck being a reflection of you,&quot; and literally became something else.<br /> <br /> It would also explain one of the features of the Strix that really struck me when I first read their chapter; it's almost impossible to bind them to anything (to their words, to some action, or an object) Their natures/essence includes immediate short-term freedom.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T17:36:18-08:00","id":1349472,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of the Strix perhaps at least having some sort of connection to Owl in the Border Marches. <br /> <br /> I think the Tokyo write-up in Werewolf 2e does mention the Strix (or tengu) have a strange interest in the Gauntlet. It might just be that the shadow realm of Dis was \u201cclose\u201d to Pangaea in the same sense you might say Inferno is \u201cclose\u201d to the Shadow or Duat is \u201cclose\u201d to the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T18:10:25-08:00","id":1349478,"title":"","content":"Worth pointing out is that the point of hypothetical divergence between Strix and humankind is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_human_prehistory\" target=\"_blank\">well before the Sundering</a>, which itself is right on the border of recorded human history \u2014 if the nature of <i>the entire interface between Earth and Shadow</i> can change as drastically as it did in five thousand years, it's certainly within reason for prehistoric human spirits to change into things dramatically different from spirits in ten times that amount of time, particularly given that the Visitors have had &quot;used to be spirits, are now much weirder&quot; as an origin point within the last century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T23:48:29-08:00","id":1349789,"title":"","content":"Just got caught up on the thread holy crap all your ideas are great! <br /> <br /> I had a similar idea where the strix came from the pangean owl, escaping to Dis to flee from father wolf. I do not know if they are linked to the the first vampires and vampirism, but they maybee taught or their knowledge was stolen by the first man who wanted cheat death and become the first vampire. Maybe mekhet? And from their vampires evolved and Strix hold a grudge? <br /> <br /> I like to think strix are beast without the bodies of a vampire as a prison, and vampires without beast are the VII. But then does that mean the VII are free from their banes, walk in the sun and do not fear fire but still poses the powers of kindred, and what pushes them to kill other kindred and to still be tied to the strix?<br /> <br /> On the note of arkadia, could the changeling arkadia be a aedes or a verge from the supernal created when the fae fled the invasion of the exarch? I still think they are one and the same in my head canon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}